            <ArticleTitle>Diffuse vasospasm following stenting of a free gastroepiploic artery graft: resolution with balloon angioplasty and intensive medical therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>352-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Vasospasm following balloon angioplasty of gastroepiploic artery bypass grafts can be prevented or reversed with vasodilators. In our patient, stent deployment for ostial stenosis of a free gastroepiploic artery graft was accompanied by severe, diffuse spasm and a change in graft configuration that required both intensive medical therapy and balloon angioplasty for resolution.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
